Vectorized packed-int4 staging in the verify attention.

The per-element path loads one byte per dim, with two threads loading the same
byte, so a warp covers 16 useful bytes per transaction and the KV loop runs
latency-bound. Here each thread loads two 4-byte words of one row (16 dims) and
stores 16 halves, so the lanes of a warp cover two complete 128-byte rows per
load instruction. 4-byte alignment holds for both caches: the row stride is 264
bytes and the V view is offset by 132.

